Z||000000||BENGAL4||01-16-2000||10:27 PM||||I am wanting a 3800 series II swap and I was wondering what other companies, besides ACE,does this. I think I could do it myself, but I know it would take all spring and summer because I am involved with my kids sports teams. Any suggestions? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||olympic||01-16-2000||11:47 PM||||   I've looked at these kits and I think that if you have access to a garage with some good tools and equipment I'd say do it yourself. Most of these swaps bolt up with very few mods or fabrication. One of the most difficult parts would be the wiring.  You can sent both harnesses away and they will join them for you so all you do is plug and go.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||01-17-2000||01:29 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A> <P>There are about 4 links covering the 3800 swap real close to the top of the list.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||01-17-2000||10:30 PM||||Probably a good bet to find someone other than ACE. (Not a fan)  Chris West is an excellent resource when it comes to custom fabrications for all kinds of swaps. (West Coast Fieros)  BTW, Chris, if you read this, thanks to you I jinxd my engine when we were picking up my dads 3.8sc red 86 GT.  You offered to 3.8 my gold 86 GT and I said I wasn't going to touch it until it shrapneled. Well, 3 & 1/2 hours and 350 miles later... (poof!!)||||reg||1
